smd_op_c5_adsr_release (opcode 0xC5) -- ADSR2 release modifier.
Disasm: lhu v0,0x4(a2); ori v0,v0,0x80; sh v0,0x4(a2); sh v1,0x2e(a2);
sh v1,0x6a(a2). Walker fans out via FUN_8001BAB8 (ADSR2-low writer):
  ADSR2 = (existing & 0xFFC0) | ((release_byte | mode_a3) & 0x3F)
Mode a3 derives from slot+0x58: ==7 → 0x20 (release_mode_exp);
else 0 (linear). MUSIC_ITER23 finding (ADSR2_RELEASE_MODE_BIT5):
on MUSIC_28, every paired ADSR2_low write had bit 5 inverted from
PCSX (PCSX=exp, Godot=linear) -- linear decay keeps voices louder
longer, producing rms_ratio=1.0873. The fix lever is upstream of
this handler in slot+0x58 selector state.
